Normally, when you use ftpmail, the files are split into pieces that are
smaller than about 60KB. Therefore, you have to concatenate the pieces
together in the right order. In the "Subject" line of the mail, the part
number should be given. The first part has a "begin" line, the last part
has an "end" line for uudecode.
Of course, you'll also have to remove the mail headers/trailers in each part.
I used a little shell script xgarbo.csh with sed to do this.
e.g. (assuming that the parts are name p01,...p0n in right order):
( call xgarbo.csh p0? )
	# (cshell)
	foreach file ( $* )
	sed -f rm_mail_signs < $file > tmp_$file
	/bin/rm $file
	end

	cat tmp_* > uu_file
	uudecode uu_file
	/bin/rm tmp_* uu_file
and the contents of the file rm_mail_signs is 
	1,/--- start/d
	/--- end/,$d

But recently, someone somewhere posted UUSHRED which is smart
enough for many cases to do the same job almost automatically.
